          "Mamallapuram",
          "Xuanzang"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "Harshavardhana ruled north India from Kannauj in the 7th century. The Chinese traveller Xuanzang visited his court.\nIn the south, the Pallavas ruled from Kanchipuram. King Narasimhavarman built the rock-cut temples and monolithic rathas at Mamallapuram.\nTheir art and architecture influenced the later Chola temples."
        }
